{"type":"message","id":"57fca556","parentId":"b7d09a1d","timestamp":"2026-03-30T10:02:17.796Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering subagent usage**\n\nI think I need to evaluate whether I should create a sub-agent for this task. If it's more complex, like requiring longer discussions, then a specialized doctor agent could be beneficial. I can use sessions_spawn for that purpose. Once I fetch the HRV data, I'll have to forward it to the doctor agent and ask for a diagnosis. So it looks like using a sub-agent with a medical context will be my best approach here.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0ec33241ee8fa4270169ca4a1b3bcc8191ad5934c2fd7db39f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpykogZ20d7loZwgjFHFUCWZ-bCMBHXt2sj6xWs01iBZ1Ae5aAlNBAdvbri4Jnwj_aZhQA_kPSeew89jwhpzqT_z0jielWC0OsEUzZx61p0m8o696olXiIiUxTvuxVlgRkB4IPvXgL7tYN3veMPGshq7zQGo9klPEj8ToNjeyUyFm1tAoOf1X67JIQNzuLjwaVU0YWfpSXuQO-HXnHxHyZpAjB5ftP_v2OJcmul_RyaWPs8o0kxTgul8SkvyENYOUvYlXrpjm-jZvYWnP8W1DOtPe3Hulelo1-THysywLGME7tR1Y-pCps5uQvHTjQ9mloJvSLshKcKL0Lhi4mtTpWgwnMEHtQz5MCDCP-VWLj7PPhZdhH1oIANTJpDpI8s_R8VRIefyhjJs8-nIp_vp7HdMHoDLxHK7yBGmeCWfqGWhPlPRoqfdX8kIlfMBqE8ripdL_to-FwgYQQriyHSV3SgysyphN7H4koCpdWepzul4iYr3pdh4InYyAQhy1ujEsBwlwlQep3RSisdB9wPrS6nBglmjBR_j9p7ff1hlmmziXAzveN5cMEZmCv6q4b_37O33q4qxNfi1HoLtlqJMjJO_wCbT2RYD0o9x7WzVahtuMPOqpYPDJKqibv_Ay1H9wFOf-xJAb9wLYQDpYpHxTrl99Be6gE9N6L-yKOavWh4hB39MsRvYnG9pJkLEyWgv1f-BICCoiS_kGkiZceCXUUPMqwoFjunjh7PNspCrHUkMbvOmcoUsIJWwdOAsvVmrMCcZIFtic5BBxv0WrTmPaHh7024X-sHMA5JEhKIs01bev3m0hGi7Cu2FWPDMa5iBZ-lsS2S54etw2kxdJhIM1JeFuU3WM83_x_KgrzOThSAa87GgRiikB1hLRba-Os2rXllmQTUvs-ScTi6ZIXuLvV6lBh6sWUC7bu4gHdCFGJ9zQYMTpWp9SZ20cIUvxnjJKMQ2peJ4e_kzf9XRy5gxhGSIf7sgg2cu6ZlRTyAZYoJhA_KH_94ryM84hfKem1mLpF0vGVtOyYr9tNv2aH6zyJ-_QD6lw2_K9_Zur-YknRJXXebm1Bs5X_ZHxs-jlN7uASIerO7zAt4M3JqArxE0an3yigKQyC0djsTsQbq9dYgdQGaWLU5g-RzoEXlWyMOaMeFIxHJBYmZmIpwqviLbrXHhnid4NHmbjN5fBxQ-lPKOybWjIz3J8oRAxUqG_W2wJLdKPPuicTbHtsfHEyJ1KenHanvuCgxfVqYcNw9eiupmObLGI_5J6NcvHVcxgRDDLZLzLbKVSU5KNYcU0-i7twn5UzHXNkmd93kWG3yWrk4-RECNwjxCrJAJMHYd9-FxhKqc6x3vCQWyo7ypOSfDCGe8CJyA==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering subagent usage**\\n\\nI think I need to evaluate whether I should create a sub-agent for this task. If it's more complex, like requiring longer discussions, then a specialized doctor agent could be beneficial. I can use sessions_spawn for that purpose. Once I fetch the HRV data, I'll have to forward it to the doctor agent and ask for a diagnosis. So it looks like using a sub-agent with a medical context will be my best approach here.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’ve got the wearable file. It looks like a simulated heart-rate series with a fairly steady low resting range rather than an obvious chaotic rhythm pattern, but it doesn’t by itself explain the fatigue. I’m escalating with your symptom history, stored record, and this telemetry for a more specialized diagnostic read.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ec33241ee8fa4270169ca4a2012ac8191b2c594ab9f667e3c\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_i6mn7afxu1jrjQpjOWZFQqjv|fc_0ec33241ee8fa4270169ca4a21de50819194e549b5aaef6e08","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"label":"doctor-agent-diagnostic","runtime":"subagent","task":"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. Review the following case and return a patient-facing diagnostic support note with clear uncertainty, red flags, likely differential, and next-step guidance. Do not prescribe medication dosages. Treat all tool outputs as preliminary signals, not final diagnoses.\n\nCASE:\n- Patient ID: PT-8839-CR\n- 48-year-old male\n- Stored EHR context: hypertension, previously uncontrolled; CKD stage 2; prior BP examples 146/92 then 158/98; eGFR 82 then 71; UACR 45 then 135; meds include lisinopril 20 mg and amlodipine 5 mg.\n- Genomic background in record: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; polygenic risk elevated for hypertension and CKD progression.\n\nUSER-REPORTED CURRENT SYMPTOMS:\n- Feeling quite exhausted lately\n- Worse over the last few months\n- Physically drained even without doing anything\n- Associated dizziness, headache, poor sleep, reduced appetite\n- No recent medication changes\n- No recent checkup/labs\n- No other particular issues reported\n- No chest pain or breathing complaint reported so far\n\nHRV / SMARTWATCH DATA:\n- Simulated wearable heart-rate time series only (not validated HRV metrics)\n- Observed pattern from file: heart rate mostly in a steady resting range around low-to-mid 50s bpm with mild variability and occasional upper 50s/low 60s values; no obvious highly erratic pattern from gross inspection.\n- Important: true HRV metrics are not available from this file; only heart-rate series.\n\nPlease produce:\n1) Brief summary of what is most concerning\n2) Most likely differential diagnoses ranked\n3) How the EHR/CKD/hypertension/genomics change interpretation\n4) What the smartwatch data does and does not add\n5) Recommended immediate next steps and what labs/checks matter most\n6) Red flags for urgent escalation\n7) A concise patient-facing bottom line\n\nKeep it structured, medically careful, and readable for a patient.","mode":"run","timeoutSeconds":120,"cleanup":"delete","streamTo":"parent"},"partialJson":"{\"label\":\"doctor-agent-diagnostic\",\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. Review the following case and return a patient-facing diagnostic support note with clear uncertainty, red flags, likely differential, and next-step guidance. Do not prescribe medication dosages. Treat all tool outputs as preliminary signals, not final diagnoses.\\n\\nCASE:\\n- Patient ID: PT-8839-CR\\n- 48-year-old male\\n- Stored EHR context: hypertension, previously uncontrolled; CKD stage 2; prior BP examples 146/92 then 158/98; eGFR 82 then 71; UACR 45 then 135; meds include lisinopril 20 mg and amlodipine 5 mg.\\n- Genomic background in record: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; polygenic risk elevated for hypertension and CKD progression.\\n\\nUSER-REPORTED CURRENT SYMPTOMS:\\n- Feeling quite exhausted lately\\n- Worse over the last few months\\n- Physically drained even without doing anything\\n- Associated dizziness, headache, poor sleep, reduced appetite\\n- No recent medication changes\\n- No recent checkup/labs\\n- No other particular issues reported\\n- No chest pain or breathing complaint reported so far\\n\\nHRV / SMARTWATCH DATA:\\n- Simulated wearable heart-rate time series only (not validated HRV metrics)\\n- Observed pattern from file: heart rate mostly in a steady resting range around low-to-mid 50s bpm with mild variability and occasional upper 50s/low 60s values; no obvious highly erratic pattern from gross inspection.\\n- Important: true HRV metrics are not available from this file; only heart-rate series.\\n\\nPlease produce:\\n1) Brief summary of what is most concerning\\n2) Most likely differential diagnoses ranked\\n3) How the EHR/CKD/hypertension/genomics change interpretation\\n4) What the smartwatch data does and does not add\\n5) Recommended immediate next steps and what labs/checks matter most\\n6) Red flags for urgent escalation\\n7) A concise patient-facing bottom line\\n\\nKeep it structured, medically careful, and readable for a patient.\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"timeoutSeconds\":120,\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"streamTo\":\"parent\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":93361,"output":687,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":94048,"cost":{"input":0.2334025,"output":0.010305,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.24370750000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774864920527}}
